      "title": "Marketing to seniors",
      "narration": "Selling to Dennis and Gloria draws extra scrutiny. Maryland’s Medicare supplement rules require advertising to be filed with the Insurance Commissioner before use and prohibit cold lead devices, which are mailings that hide their insurance purpose, high-pressure tactics, and any suggestion of government endorsement. Twisting, misrepresentation and the use of titles implying Medicare expertise beyond a producer license are banned. Producers must make reasonable efforts to determine that a policy is appropriate: it may not duplicate Medicare, an Advantage plan or another supplement, and it may not be sold to someone on Medicaid except in narrow cases. Excessive insurance is itself a violation.",
