      "narration": "Beyond the federal six-month open enrollment at 65, Maryland adds protections. People under 65 who qualify for Medicare because of disability must be offered Plans A and D for six months after Part B enrollment, and the Plan A premium may not exceed the average paid by policyholders 65 and older. Since July 1, 2023, Maryland has a birthday rule: for 30 days after each birthday, an existing policyholder may switch to a policy with equal or lesser benefits from any insurer without underwriting, and insurers must give notice of that right 30 to 60 days before the birthday. Group supplements that end must offer individual conversion, and continuation applies when membership ends.",
